# Autoclip app (installs on your phone, no Termux)

Files: index.html, style.css, app.js, config.js, sw.js, manifest.webmanifest, icons/

## Install on your phone
1. Put all these files in one folder on a free https host (GitHub Pages, Cloudflare Pages or Netlify).
2. Open the https address in Chrome > menu (three dots) > Install app / Add to Home screen.
3. To update later, upload the new files over the old ones, then open the app and refresh it twice.

## Links from YouTube, Instagram, Facebook and others
Links are downloaded by your own online Autoclip server (see the autoclip-server zip for steps).
In the app tap "Server settings", enter your server address (for example https://autoclip-xxxx.onrender.com)
and your access key. The address is remembered. You can also put it in config.js.
Without a server you can still choose a video file from your phone.

## Choosing clips
After the clips are found, tick the ones you want and tap "Export selected". Tap Edit to preview or change a clip.
Exported clips are saved in My clips inside the app and downloaded to your phone.

## Notes
- Projects and saved clips stay inside the app on your phone until you delete them.
- Exports record each clip in real time at 1080p. Keep the app open while it works.
- Auto-generate captions needs Chrome speech recognition and may not work in a plain APK wrapper.
